cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or the released data splits, please cite this record."
type: software
title: "CMGNet-SPrompt: a deep learning framework for quinolone scaffold detection in cosmetics via 13C NMR spectroscopy"
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-11-16
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/LingjieBao1998/NMR_CMGNet_SPrompt"
keywords:
  - 13C NMR
  - quinolone
  - scaffold detection
  - molecular generation
  - cosmetic adulteration
  - deep learning
abstract: >-
  CMGNet-SPrompt combines a conditional BART-based molecular generator with a
  CReSS/XGBoost scaffold gate to detect the 4-oxo-1,4-dihydroquinoline-3-carboxylic
  acid core from pure 13C NMR peak lists.  The release contains training and
  inference code, the processed data splits, figure-generation scripts and the
  reported model checkpoints.
